# Ownership of *results* is not expressed here on purpose.
#
# A result file belongs to the contributor whose login is in `provenance.github_login`, and
# that is enforced by `tools/validate` on every pull request (SPEC §5.3) rather than by a
# review requirement: a repository-wide owner for `results/` would put one person in the
# path of every measurement anybody ever submits, which is exactly the bottleneck this
# project is built to avoid.
#
# What does need a maintainer's eye is everything a result is *interpreted* against: a wrong
# memory bandwidth or a wrong engine default silently invalidates measurements that were
# themselves correct.

/schemas/            @0xBakeer
/hardware/           @0xBakeer
/models/             @0xBakeer
/engines/            @0xBakeer
/workloads/          @0xBakeer
/datasets/           @0xBakeer
/site/               @0xBakeer

/packages/           @0xBakeer
/tools/              @0xBakeer
/app/                @0xBakeer
/bench/              @0xBakeer
/.github/            @0xBakeer
/docs/               @0xBakeer
/AGENTS.md           @0xBakeer
/CONTRIBUTING.md     @0xBakeer

# results/ — deliberately unowned; see above.
